  {
    "labelChirho": "Nathan (personal name)",
    "descriptionChirho": "Proper masculine name meaning 'he gave', referring primarily to the prophet Nathan who confronted David about Bathsheba (2 Sam 7,12) and supported Solomon's succession (1 Kgs 1), as well as Nathan son of David (2 Sam 5:14) and other figures. Transliterated uniformly: eng 'Nathan/Natan', spa 'Natán/Natan', arb 'ناثان', kor '나단', swa 'Nathani', hin 'नातान'. The two clusters differ only in grammatical context (with/without conjunction and preposition), not in referent or meaning.",
